{"repositoryId":9028617,"availability":"available","full":"LanguageMachines/ucto","name":"ucto","description":"Unicode tokeniser. Ucto tokenizes text files: it separates words from punctuation, and splits sentences. It offers several other basic preprocessing steps such as changing case that you can all use to make your text suited for further processing such as indexing, part-of-speech tagging, or machine translation.  Ucto comes with tokenisation rules for several languages and can be easily extended to suit other languages. It has been incorporated for tokenizing Dutch text in Frog, our Dutch morpho-syntactic processor. http://ilk.uvt.nl/ucto --","category":"Developer tools","language":"C++","stars":72,"forks":14,"created":"2013-03-26T11:16:57Z","updated":"2026-08-20T10:11:43Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://languagemachines.github.io/ucto","topics":["computational-linguistics","folia","language","natural-language-processing","nlp","punctuation","tokeniser"],"demo":"https://languagemachines.github.io/ucto","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:41:59.574Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T09:41:59.574Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T09:41:59.574Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:41:59.574Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"curated-list","name":"Awesome Machine Learning","url":"https://github.com/josephmisiti/awesome-machine-learning"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T09:41:59.574Z","stars":72,"forks":14}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ucto tokenizes text files: it separates words from punctuation, and splits sentences. This is one of the first tasks for almost any Natural Language Processing application. Ucto offers several other basic preprocessing steps such as changing case that you can all use to make your text suited for further processing such as indexing, part-of-speech tagging, or machine translation.","Ucto comes with tokenisation rules for several languages (packaged separately) and can be easily extended to suit other languages. It has been incorporated for tokenizing Dutch text in Frog ( our Dutch morpho-syntactic processor.","The software is intended to be used from the command-line by researchers in Natural Language Processing or related areas, as well as software developers. An Ucto python binding is also available separately."],"features":["Comes with tokenization rules for English, Dutch, French, Italian, Turkish,","Recognizes units, currencies, abbreviations, and simple dates and times like dd-mm-yyyy","Recognizes paired quote spans, sentences, and paragraphs.","Produces UTF8 encoding and NFC output normalization, optionally accepting","Ligature normalization (can undo for isntance fi,fl as single codepoints)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LanguageMachines/ucto/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"037a716773fb6f3ec7dedc89294e112d68e140a5fe03585684e26b8b89377ab3","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T09:41:59.574Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:41:59.574Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Ucto tokenizes text files: it separates words from punctuation, and splits sentences. This is one of the first tasks for almost any Natural Language Processing application. Ucto offers several other basic preprocessing steps such as changing case that you can all use to make your text suited for further processing such as indexing, part-of-speech tagging, or machine translation.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LanguageMachines/ucto/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Ucto tokenizes text files: it separates words from punctuation, and splits sentences. This is one of the first tasks for almost any Natural Language Processing application. Ucto offers several other basic preprocessing steps such as changing case that you can all use to make your text suited for further processing such as indexing, part-of-speech tagging, or machine…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LanguageMachines/ucto/blob/master/README.md"}],"re